    description: "Add a canonical content digest (sha256 over the volatile-stripped / `--reproducible` survey) to the top-level survey envelope. An `# axis: identity` field: two runs on identical code share a digest; any semantic change flips it. Gives O(1) \"same survey?\" plus the natural diff / cache key.\n\nProcedurally lightweight per ADR-0024 / ADR-0033: it is an `identity` field, so no new registry / axis machinery is required. Must hash a stable, volatile-stripped form -> requires the `--reproducible` byte-repro mode first.\n\nBeyond G8 / WI-pifaj scope: new aijo-layer work; no canonical digest exists today (2026-07-21 G8 verification). Demand-gated on aijo. Blocks: survey diff. Blocked-by: the `--reproducible` mode."  # e5f0
